{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen","id":719422,"title":"What Are the Huntsmen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T08:52:16-07:00","id":719422,"title":"What Are the Huntsmen?","content":"I often forget to check the front page news, so it's possible I may have missed this.<br /> <br /> But do we actually know what the Huntsmen are supposed to be at this point? Are they the new version of loyalists (i.e Changelings that serve the Keeper), or are they a completely different species like the Hobgoblins? The Lost seem terrified of them, which if they were just simple Changelings, shouldn't be that big of a deal. So I'm a little curious about the subject.<br /> <br /> If they're loyalists, I'd like to think it would be possible to play a Huntsman chronicle, but if they're something else completely, it would be nice to know what they're capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:30:15-07:00","id":719614,"title":"","content":"They are [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> Isn't that exciting?!<br /> <br /> EDIT: More seriously, beyond what the Outline told us, Dave has not announced anything on the Huntsmen. I will say they are my new favorite enemy of Changeling, supplanting Fetches. Nothing more can be said until Dave decides to chat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-23-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:40:31-07:00","id":719657,"title":"","content":"What we know from the outline is that they are agents in the employ of the True Fae, and that they can look like anything. Your toaster might be a huntsman in disguise. But that's about all we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:04:36-07:00","id":719734,"title":"","content":"i figured they were hedge beasts with shapeshifting powers and the ability to track you down via an icon, with the disadvantage of having to work within your approach. but we dont actually know for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:08:14-07:00","id":719743,"title":"","content":"Since everything else is stuff that's been trickled, I'm curious how you reached the conclusion of hedge beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:51:39-07:00","id":719886,"title":"","content":"Oh right, the outline, lets see.<br /> <br /> They're free agents. 'They seek out threads of the Lost in the Hedge.' They can look like anything, as has been pointed out above, they're not 'that' scary as combatants, but they're scary as hunters. They trap and use your environment and allies against you. And they have Arcadian weapons, which sound cool.<br /> <br /> That summarized from the outline, which may be out of date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T11:35:22-07:00","id":719974,"title":"","content":"Nah, everything mentioned in there is still applicable.<br /> <br /> Arcadian weapons are nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-23-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:13:51-07:00","id":720712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=719743#post719743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since everything else is stuff that's been trickled, I'm curious how you reached the conclusion of hedge beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, I often forget to check the news. Last thing I remember hearing on Huntsmen was that they stalked Changelings and used Arcadian weapons. Anything beyond that, I haven't heard about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:19:36-07:00","id":720730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=720712#post720712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I often forget to check the news. Last thing I remember hearing on Huntsmen was that they stalked Changelings and used Arcadian weapons. Anything beyond that, I haven't heard about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very little has been revealed about them. You're about on the same page as the rest of us. Though, I wouldn't be surprised if we get to see more about them once second drafts are done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:43:25-07:00","id":720806,"title":"","content":"I was asking Nas. I'm always curious about how people reach their conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:26:45-07:00","id":720941,"title":"","content":"They are a manifestation of your mortal soul, still trapped in Arcadia by the Gentry, reaching out to reunite with you -- by bringing you back.<br /> <br /> (Or something. I made that up.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:05:37-07:00","id":721294,"title":"","content":"How'd you reach that conclusion? Again, curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:23:01-07:00","id":721353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=721294#post721294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How'd you reach that conclusion? Again, curious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the information on them says they collect the pieces you left behind, not embody them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T12:44:49-07:00","id":723982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=721294#post721294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How'd you reach that conclusion? Again, curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a conclusion. I made it up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was the first idea for &quot;nebulous thing that's after you from Arcadia&quot; that popped into my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T18:30:24-08:00","id":755510,"title":"","content":"The argument that Huntsmen may be the part of changelings that were discarded so that the changeling could escape Arcadia can be supported by these facts all the seemings sacrifice something to get back and Huntsmen gain &quot;Yearning&quot; by hunting changings in certain ways, probably a stat or condition the Huntsmen use against the changeling to make their hunt successful, which would make sense if they were part of the changing that wants to be in Arcadia or couldn't escape Arcadia and simply wants to re-unite.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yearning&quot; hasn't been defined yet, but given this supposed context the pieces fall into place neatly. Not saying it's the right conclusion, just that the pattern fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:55:24-08:00","id":757135,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting hypothesis. Though I think the piece left behind is supposed to be a Chaneling's Icon, it is a disturbing thought that a Huntsman might not just have <i>taken</i> your Icon and used it to find you, but they might actually <i>be</i> your Icon coming back for you itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:30:46-08:00","id":757623,"title":"","content":"I was hoping they were actual Changelings. I like playing a villain game now and then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T19:44:06-08:00","id":757768,"title":"","content":"Can't you do that as a Loyalist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:56:41-08:00","id":757873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=757768#post757768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you do that as a Loyalist?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure if Loyalists are in 2nd edition. I thought they were replaced with Huntsmen, since they pretty much do the same thing from what I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T21:09:26-08:00","id":757903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=757873#post757873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Loyalists are in 2nd edition. I thought they were replaced with Huntsmen, since they pretty much do the same thing from what I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Okay, you appear to be doing approximately three different things here, none of which are wise.<br /> <br /> 1. Conflating loyalists and privateers despite there being something like three different book writeups that discuss how they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> 2. Treating sporadic discussion of how Huntsmen can take some of the narrative load off of loyalists and the Fae themselves by virtue of being neither sort of fae with some kind of dev/writer statement that Huntsmen replace loyalists (since they can't wholly replace the Fae).<br /> <br /> 3. Not rereading <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the outline</a> that gives loyalists as an explicit and separate section of the Antagonists chapter from the one that the Huntsmen get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T21:14:42-08:00","id":757909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=757903#post757903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Okay, you appear to be doing approximately three different things here, none of which are wise.<br /> <br /> 1. Conflating loyalists and privateers despite there being something like three different book writeups that discuss how they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> 2. Treating sporadic discussion of how Huntsmen can take some of the narrative load off of loyalists and the Fae themselves by virtue of being neither sort of fae with some kind of dev/writer statement that Huntsmen replace loyalists (since they can't wholly replace the Fae).<br /> <br /> 3. Not rereading <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the outline</a> that gives loyalists as an explicit and separate section of the Antagonists chapter from the one that the Huntsmen get.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What are you talking about 3 different books? I thought 2nd edition was still in development and that Huntsmen were something new to it. Also, Privateers (as I understand it) are Changelings who hunt and capture other Changelings. While Loyalists are Changelings who work for the Fae. Not really much of a difference there.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I don't really buy the supplement books, just the core book and the rule book. Personally I feel like there's way too many supplements to keep track of anymore. My dad used to be really into D&amp;D and had like a stack of about 10 different books for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:07:11-08:00","id":758006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=757909#post757909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you talking about 3 different books? I thought 2nd edition was still in development and that Huntsmen were something new to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loyalists and privateers both exist in first edition. The corebook almost categorically mentions them as a separate category of threat from loyalists and Fae, Autumn Nightmares' first chapter opens its &quot;Privateers and Loyalists&quot; section with a direct discussion of the distinction between the two, and Hunter's Mortal Remains supplement has a section on the two in its Changelings chapter that specifically talks about the differences:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Lost would do almost anything to avoid returning to Arcadia. Some Changelings, however, would do truly anything \u2014 including selling others to that fate \u2014 to avoid being subjugated again. Privateers are much worse; they capture other humans and Changelings for profit and send them off to Arcadia. The word \u201cprivateer\u201d is a polite name other Changelings use to call these wretched traitors. Generally speaking, privateers are Lost who use their fae-born abilities to capture, sell, and enslave humans and Changelings. Privateers take their kidnapped victims through the Hedge and sell them to Goblin Market slave stall owners \u2014 or even to the True Fae themselves.<br /> <br /> Most Changelings believe that the only thing worse than a privateer is a loyalist \u2014 a Lost who continues to work for a True Fae\u2019s interests, even after her release back into the human world. Some loyalists serve out of a misguided sense of duty; others are bound by magical ties, supernatural oaths, or are being coerced in other ways. The most unforgiveable loyalists sell out their fellow Lost because they can\u2019t turn down the True Fae\u2019s offer for power, wealth, or pleasure.<br /> <br /> Not all privateers are loyalists; some Changelings are motivated by profit and hate the True Fae. Not all loyalists are privateers, either; they may also serve the True Fae as spies or exotic goods dealers, too. Those who fall into both groups are the bane of the Lost\u2019s existence. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Privateers (as I understand it) are Changelings who hunt and capture other Changelings. While Loyalists are Changelings who work for the Fae. Not really much of a difference there. </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between a mercenary and a spy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:37:10-08:00","id":758541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=758006#post758006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loyalists and privateers both exist in first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I knew that. But from what we've heard about Huntsmen being that they hunt and capture escaped Lost and they infiltrate the Freeholds by exploiting certain rituals, it sounds like they're replacing the Privateer function. That's what I'm confused about, since it sounded like they might be a new name for the same thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:56:21-08:00","id":758592,"title":"","content":"Privateers still exist. Huntsmen do not replace them-in fact, it would be wise of a Huntsman to hire a few privateers while they are out and about to back up their own talents and those of any Loyalists the Stranger gives them.<br /> <br /> But, for what it's worth, I would rather love being able to have the occasional Huntsmen game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-06-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:22:40-08:00","id":758621,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. :P<br /> <br /> Thinking back on it now, didn't it say they can look like anything? Which could imply they have physical characteristics normal Lost don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:25:34-08:00","id":758626,"title":"","content":"By the way, if any mods are reading this, it seems the spam bot is back. This time they've over at Scion going by the name of Arina. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:27:24-08:00","id":758629,"title":"","content":"I think I once said there are about four major things that make up the aesthetic of a Huntsmen when they aren't being all sneaky sneaky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:04:06-08:00","id":758837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/719422-what-are-the-huntsmen?p=758592#post758592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, for what it's worth, I would rather love being able to have the occasional Huntsmen game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Late to the party, but do you mean playing AS a Huntsman? As in, that may be possible in the system? Or am I misreading this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:07:41-08:00","id":758846,"title":"","content":"Technically, anything is possible. Playing an Ephemeral Being, for example, might be difficult, but with sufficient effort it could be doable. If I remember correctly Geist actually suggested that some players in the group play the Geists of another member of the group, and in Mummy they have some Numina and rules that could enable the playing of Revenants or the Lucid Dead. Some of the Promethean supplements reference the 'player' of a Pandoran or <i>Sublimatus</i>. Equinox Road gives you the option of becoming one of the Gentry. Not too far of a stretch to do something like try and play a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:28:14-08:00","id":758894,"title":"","content":"1) I did indeed mean play as a Huntsman.<br /> <br /> 2) It's not possible in the system as written-It's not like playing a Seer of the Throne in Mage, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:22:37-08:00","id":758989,"title":"","content":"My understanding from implied context is that Huntsmen fill the inhuman-adversary role Strix fill in Requiem, and act as a powered-appropriately-to-most-games stand-in for True Fae. Privateers have limitations of Clarity and serve as contemptible foe because you can relate to their human weaknesses that lead them to their actions, whereas Huntsmen won't have limitations of Clarity and can have motives alien to the Lost. They are monsters without mortal minds or hearts in a way similar to spirits, Strix, or True Fae themselves, or at least I hope they are. It'd be a needed dab of color for my storytelling pallet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:47:18-08:00","id":761950,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to hearing about them. I'm surprised that this hasn't been revealed by now, considering that Oynx Path was calling it 'The Huntsman Chronicles' about a year ago. Currently going through a drought of information, which is unfortunate; Lost is the main reason I poke my head into this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T20:18:55-08:00","id":761968,"title":"","conte